772: translations on the smooth model $X'\to \Delta$ over the order 
773: $3$ base change $\Delta\to \Delta_0$
774: of Corollary \ref{fill2}, 
775: which are invariant under the $\mu_3$ deck action.
776: Similarly, the finite group $\tfrac{1}{4}\Lambda^{T_1}/\Lambda^{T_1}$ consists
777: of the $4$-torsion translations on the smooth model over $\Delta\to \Delta_1$
778: which are invariant under the $\mu_4$ deck action. These torsion sections
779: play an important role in the following construction.
780: 
781: \begin{construction}[Log transform]\label{con-log}
782: Given $\overline{a}_0\in \tfrac{1}{3}
783: \Lambda^{T_0}/\Lambda^{T_0}$ we may define a twisted $\mu_3$-action $\widetilde{\rho}$ 
784: on the smooth replacement $X'\to \Delta$ (Corollary \ref{fill2}) of 
785: the base change $X(u)\times_{\Delta_0} \Delta$ by setting $$\widetilde{\rho}(x) = \rho(x) + 
786: \overline{a}_0.$$ Here $\rho$ denotes the deck action induced on the chosen
787: smooth extension $X'$. Over the punctured disk, its
788: quotient identifies with $X(u)|_{\Delta_0^*}$.
789: We may then form the twisted quotient
790: $$X'/\langle \widetilde{\rho}\rangle.$$ 
791: We require the following lemma: 
792: 
793: \begin{lemma}\label{twist} 
794: The twisted quotient $X'/\langle \widetilde{\rho}\rangle$ is biholomorphic
795: over the punctured neighborhood $\Delta_0^*$ to $X(u)\vert_{\Delta_0^*}$. Furthermore,
796: a lift of $\overline{a}_0$ to some $a_0\in \tfrac{1}{3}\Lambda^{T_0}$ determines
797: explicitly such a biholomorphism.
798: \end{lemma}
799: 
800: \begin{proof}
801: Put $v_0=3a_0\in\Lambda^{T_0}$ and choose the generator of the deck group
802: so that it acts on the base by $s\mapsto\zeta_3s$.  Over $\Delta^*$ define
803: the section
804: $$
805: \sigma_{a_0}(s)=\frac{\log s}{2\pi i}v_0
806: =\frac{3\log s}{2\pi i}a_0.
807: $$
808: Although $\log s$ is multivalued, moving to a new branch changes
809: $\sigma_{a_0}$ by an integral multiple of $v_0\in\Lambda$.  It therefore
810: defines a single-valued holomorphic section of the family of complex tori
811: over $\Delta^*$.  Let
812: $$
813: \Psi_{a_0}(x,s)=(x+\sigma_{a_0}(s),s)
814: $$
815: be translation by this section.
816: 
817: Since $v_0$ is fixed by $T_0$, analytic continuation gives
818: $$
819: \sigma_{a_0}(\zeta_3 s)
820: =T_0^{-1}\sigma_{a_0}(s)+a_0.
821: $$
822: Consequently,
823: $$
824: \Psi_{a_0}\circ\rho
825: =\widetilde\rho\circ\Psi_{a_0}.
826: $$
827: Thus $\Psi_{a_0}$ descends to a biholomorphism between the quotients by
828: $\rho$ and $\widetilde\rho$ over $\Delta_0^*$.  The quotient by $\rho$ is
829: $X(u)\vert_{\Delta_0^*}$ which proves the lemma. \end{proof}
830: 
831: There is an exactly analogous construction given an element 
832: $\overline{a}_1\in \tfrac{1}{4}\Lambda^{T_1}/\Lambda^{T_1}$ 
833: and a lift $a_1\in \tfrac{1}{4}\Lambda^{T_1}$. The $a_i$ encode the ``multiplicity
834: class'' of \cite[Def.~5.22]{EFGMS25}.
835: 
836: \begin{definition} We define the analytic space $X(u,a_0,a_1)$ by gluing to
837: $X(u)\vert_{\bP^1\setminus \{0,1\}}$ the twisted quotients of Lemma~\ref{twist}
838: associated to $a_0\in \tfrac{1}{3}\Lambda^{T_0}$ and
839: $a_1\in \tfrac{1}{4}\Lambda^{T_1}$. \end{definition}
840: \end{construction}
841: 
842: \begin{lemma}\label{covect}
843: The space of globally monodromy-invariant linear functionals $\Lambda\to \bZ$ 
844: has rank $1$, generated by the map
845: $\psi\colon \Lambda\to \bZ$ of (\ref{filt1}). \end{lemma}
846: 
847: \begin{proof} This is immediate from the monodromy
848: matrices $[T_0]_{\cB_0}$, $[T_1]_{\cB_1}$, and change of basis $C$
849: computed in Theorem \ref{matrices}.
850: \end{proof}
851: 
852: We will see the significance of this global invariant covector in the course of the proof of the main theorem.
853: 
854: 
855: \begin{corollary}\label{biell}
856: When $a_0$ and $a_1$ satisfy
857: $\psi(a_0)\in \tfrac{1}{3}\bZ\setminus \bZ$, $\psi(a_1)\in \tfrac{1}{4}\bZ\setminus \tfrac{1}{2}\bZ$,
858: the twisted action of $\widetilde{\rho}$ on $X'_i$, for $i=0,1$, is free. Thus
859: $X(u,a_0,a_1)\to \bP^1$ has the following multiple fibers:
860: \begin{enumerate} 
861: \item multiplicity $3$ over $0$, with reduced fiber a bielliptic surface of
862: Bagnera--de Franchis type $\mu_3\times \mu_3$.\smallskip
863: \item multiplicity $4$ over $1$, with reduced fiber a bielliptic surface of
864: Bagnera--de Franchis type $\mu_2\times \mu_4$.
865: \end{enumerate}
866:  \end{corollary}
867: 
868: See \cite[Ch.~V, \S 5]{BHPV04} for the classification of bielliptic surfaces.
869:  
870:  \begin{proof}
871: This follows from the description of the abelian surfaces
872: $F_0$ and $F_1$ in Corollary \ref{fill} and 
873: of the twisted action in Construction \ref{con-log}.
874: The covector $\psi$ induces a map $F_i\to \bR/\bZ$, 
875: on which the twisted action is translation by $\psi(a_i)$. By hypothesis, 
876: this translation has exact order $3$, respectively $4$. 
877: Thus every nonidentity element acts without fixed points, so the action is free.
878:  \end{proof}
